{#
 # One row.
 #
 # `split` pushes the row's two sides apart — something on the left, something on the right.
 #
 # `label` is the shorthand for the common case: a key/value row, whose left side is a word. Pass
 # `split` on its own when the left side is richer than a word — a medal and a name on a podium — since
 # `label` is plain text and rendering markup through it would mean trusting it.
 #
 # The two do not share a layout. `split` throws its sides to opposite edges, which is right for a
 # podium: the name grows, the figure stays at the end of the row, and the card is narrow. A pair reads
 # as a pair only while its halves are within a glance of each other, and `space-between` across
 # /profile's 1006 px at 1920 put « Nom » and its value 889 px apart. So a pair gives its key a column
 # of its own and starts the value right after it — see components/_list-group.scss.
 #
 # `label` is named after `Table:Cell`'s prop on purpose: same idea, same word.
 #
 # `emphasis` is the row a list adds up to — the total under its lines. `muted` is a row whose value
 # is an absence rather than a figure.
 #
 # A row is never a link. The kit this follows offers that, at the price of the whole list becoming a
 # `div` of anchors, and the two lists that hold links here — a member's groups, a group's members —
 # read perfectly well with the name as the link inside the row. A prop nobody passes is a prop
 # nobody maintains; add it back the day a row wants to be actionable as a whole.
 #}
{% props label = null, split = false, emphasis = false, muted = false %}

{%- set listGroupItem = html_cva(
    base: 'list-group-item',
    variants: {
        split: { true: 'd-flex justify-content-between' },
        pair: { true: 'app-list-pair' },
        emphasis: { true: 'fw-bold' },
        muted: { true: 'text-body-secondary' },
    },
) -%}

{%- set classes = listGroupItem.apply({
    split: split,
    pair: label is not null,
    emphasis: emphasis,
    muted: muted,
}) -%}

<li{{ attributes.defaults({ class: classes }) }}>
    {%- if label is not null %}
        <span class="app-list-key">{{ label }}</span><span class="app-list-value">
    {% endif -%}

    {%- block content %}{% endblock -%}

    {%- if label is not null %}
        </span>
    {% endif -%}
</li>
